hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1897","# Hadith Translation\n\n**Narrated by Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), who said:**\n\n\"Many among men have attained perfection, but among women, none attained perfection except Maryam, the daughter of 'Imran, and Asiyah, the wife of Pharaoh. And the superiority of 'Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) over all other women is like the superiority of *tharid* (a dish of bread and meat stew) over all other foods.\"\n\n**Additional Narrators:**\nIt is also narrated from 'Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and Anas (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\n**Classification by Abu Isa al-Tirmidhi:**\nThis is a *hasan sahih* (good and authentic) hadith.\n\n---\n\n**Notes:**\n- **Perfection (*kamal*)** in this context refers to spiritual excellence and closeness to Allah.\n- **Maryam (peace be upon her)** is the mother of Prophet Isa (Jesus, peace be upon him).\n- **Asiyah** was the wife of Pharaoh, who believed in Allah despite her husband's tyranny.\n- **Tharid** is a traditional Arabian dish considered the finest of foods, used here as a metaphor for excellence."
"1898","Ubaidullah bin 'Abdullah narrated a report (of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from Abu Sa'eed"
"1899","Narrated 'Eisa bin 'Abdullah bin Unais: From his father who said: \"I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) standing at a hanging water-skin"
"1900","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abi 'Amrah: From his grandmother Kabshah who said: \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon me. He drank from a hanging water-skin while standing. So I went to its mouth and cut it off.\" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib. Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir is the brother of 'Adbur-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir. He died earlier than him"
"1901","Narrated Anas bin Malik: \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought some milk which was mixed with some water. On his right was a Bedouin and on his left was Abu Bakr. So he drank"
"1902","Narrated Abu Qatadah: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"The one providing water for people is the last of them to drink.\" He said: There is something on this topic from Ibn Abi Awfa. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"
"1903","Narrated 'Aishah: \"The drink most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was the sweet"
"1904","Narrated Az-Zuhri: \"The Prophet (ﷺ) was asked: 'Which drink is the best ?' He said: 'The sweet"
"1905","Narrated by 'Abdah ibn 'Abdullah al-Khuza'i al-Basri, who said: narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham, from Sufyan, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \"What an excellent condiment is vinegar!\" This hadith is more authentic (aṣaḥḥ) than the hadith of Mubarak ibn Sa'id."
"1906","Ibn Mas'ud said:\"I asked the Messenger of Allah: 'O Messenger of Allah! Which is the most virtuous of deeds?' He said: 'Salat during its appropriate time.' I said: 'Then what"
"1907","Abdullah bin Amr narrated that:the Prophet said: \"The Lord's pleasure is in the parent's pleasure"
"1908","Abu 'Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami narrated from Abu Ad Darda'.:He said that a man came and said : \"I have a wife whom my mother has ordered me to divorce.\" So Abu Ad-Darda said: \" I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: 'The father is the middle gate to Paradise. So if you wish"
"1909","Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakrah narrated from his father who said:\" The messenger of Allah said: 'Shall I not tell you of the biggest of the major sins?' they said : 'Of course! O Messenger of Allah!' He said: 'To join partners with Allah"
"1910","Abdullah bin 'Amr narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \"It is among the greatest of sins that a man should curse his parents.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah! Does a man curse his parents?\" He said: \"Yes. He verbally abuses the father of a man"
"1911","Ibn 'Umar narrated that :the Prophet said: \"Among the most dutiful of deeds is that a man nurture relations with the people his father was friends with"
"1912","Al-Bara' bin Azib narrated that :the Prophet said: \"The maternal aunt holds the same status as the mother"
"1913","Abu Harairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Three supplications are accepted"
"1914","Abu Hurairah narrated that:the Messenger of Allah said: \"A son could not do enough for his father"
"1915","Abu Salamah said:\" Abu[Ar-Raddad] Al-Laithi complained(of an illness). So 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf visited him. He said: 'The best of you"
"1916","Abdullah bin Amr narrated that:the Prophet said: \"Merely maintaining the ties of kinship is not adequate. But connecting the ties of kinship is when his ties to the womb are severed and he connects it"
"1917","Narrated Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who reported from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said:\n\n\"When one of you has his servant prepare his food, enduring its heat and smoke, then let him take him by the hand and seat him beside him (to eat together). If the servant refuses, then let him take a morsel and feed it to him.\"\n\nAbu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: \"This is a hasan sahih hadith. And Abu Khalid, the father of Isma'il, is named Sa'd.\""
"1918","Yūsuf ibn Ḥammād al-Maʿnī al-Baṣrī narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Jumaḥī narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Ziyād, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said:\n\n\"Spread (the greeting of) peace, feed (others) food, and strike the heads (i.e., slaughter sacrificial animals), and you will inherit Paradise.\"\n\nHe (the narrator) said: In this chapter, there are narrations from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, Ibn ʿUmar, Anas, ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿĀʾish, and Sharīḥ ibn Hānʾ from his father.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ gharīb hadith from the narration of Ibn Ziyād from Abū Hurayrah."
"1919","Abu Hurairah narrated:\"Al-Aqra' bin Habis saw the prophet kissing Al-Hasan\"- Ibn Abi 'Umar (one of the narrators) said:\"Al-Hasan and Al-Husain.\" So he said: 'I have ten children and I do not kiss any one of them.' So the Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever shows no mercy"
"1920","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \"There is no one who has three daughters"
"1921","Aishah narrated that the:Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever is tried with something from daughters"
"1922","Abu Bakr bin 'Ubaidullah bin Anas bin Malik narrated [from Anas] that:the Messenger of Allah said: \"Whoever raises two girls then I and he will enter Paradise like these two.\" And he indicated with his two fingers"
"1923","Aishah said:\"A woman came to me with two daughters. She was asking (for food) but I did not have anything with me except a date. So I gave it to her and she divided it between her two daughters without eating any of it herself. Then she got up to leave"
"1924","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \"Whoever has three daughters"
"1925","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that:the Prophet said: Whoever takes in an orphan among the Muslims to raise"
"1926","Abu Hurairah narrated that:the Messenger of Allah said: \"The religion is An-Nasihah\" three times. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah! For Whom?\" He said : \"To Allah"
"1927","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:: \"The Muslim is the brother to the Muslim"
"1928","Abu Musa Al-Ash'arf narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:: The believer is to the believer like parts of a building"
"1929","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:: \"Indeed (each) one of you is the reflection of his brother. So if he sees something harmful in him"
"1930","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:: \"Whoever relieves a Muslim of a burden from the burdens of the world"
"1931","Abu Ad-Darda narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever protects his brother's honor"
"1932","Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:: It is not lawful for the Muslim to shun his brother for more than three (days); they come fare to fare and this one turns away"
"1933","Anas said:: \"When 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf arrived in Al-Madinah"
"1934","Abu Hurairah narrated that it was said:\" O Messenger of Allah! What is backbiting?\" He said : \" Mentioning your brother with that which he does not like.\" He said \" What if what I said about him is so?\" He said: \"If what you said about him is so"
"1935","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Do not cut off one another"
"1936","Salim narrated from his father who said that the Messenger of Allah said:\"There is to be no envy except for two: A man to whom Allah grants wealth and he spends from it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day. And a man to whom Allah grants (memorization of) the Quran so he stands with it (in prayer) during the hours of the night and the hours of the day"
"1937","Jabir narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Indeed Ash-Shaitan has despaired of getting those who perform Salat to worship him.But he is engaged in sowing hatred among them"
"1938","Umm Kulthum bint 'Uqbah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"One who brings peace between people is not a liar"
"1939","Asma bint Yazid narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"it is not lawful to lie except in three cases: Something the man tells his wife to please her"
"1940","Abu Sirmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever causes harm"
"1941","Abu Bakr As-Siddiq narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Cursed are those who harm a believer"
"1942","Aishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Jibril – may the Salawat of Allah be upon him – continued to recommend me about (treating) the neighbors so (kindly and politely)"
"1943","Mujahid narrated:\"Abdullah bin Amr had a sheep slaughtered for his family"
"1944","Abdullah bin Amr narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"The companion who is the best to Allah is the one who is best to his companion. And the neighbor that is the best to Allah is the one that is best to his neighbor"
"1945","Abu Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"Allah has made some of your brothers as slaves under your care. So whoever has his brother under his care"
"1946","Abu Bakr As-Siddiq narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"The one who treats his slaves badly will not enter paradise"
"1947","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by Ibn ʿAbbas (may Allah be pleased with them both):**\n\nThe Prophet ﷺ drank from Zamzam water while standing.\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** In this chapter, there are narrations from ʿAlī, Saʿd, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, and ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with them all).\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* (good and authentic) hadith.\n\n---\n\n**Isnād (Chain of Narration):**\n\nAḥmad ibn Manīʿ narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal and Mughīrah narrated to us — from al-Shaʿbī — from Ibn ʿAbbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) — that the Prophet ﷺ drank from Zamzam while standing."
"1948","Abu Mas'ud [Al-Ansari] said:\"I was beating a slave of mine and I heard someone behind me saying: 'Beware O Abu Mas'ud! Beware O Abu Mas'ud!' So I turned around and saw that it was the Messenger of Allah. He said: 'Allah has more power over you than you do over him.\" Abu Mas'ud said: \"I have not beaten any slave of mine since then"
"1949","Abdullah bin 'Umar narrated:\"A man came to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! How many times should the servant be pardoned?' The Prophet was silent. Then he said: 'O Messenger of Allah! How many times should the servant be pardoned?' He said: ' Seventy times each day"
"1950","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"When one of you beats his servant then he (should) remember Allah and"
"1951","Jabir bin Sumurah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"That a man should discipline his son is better for him than to have given a Sa' in charity"
"1952","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by ʿAlī ibn Khashram:** He narrated to us that ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us, from Rishdīn ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allāh be pleased with both of them), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allāh be upon him) used to breathe twice when he drank.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: This is a *gharīb* (uncommon) hadith. We do not know it except through the narration of Rishdīn ibn Kurayb.\n\nHe further said: I asked Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān [al-Dārimī] about Rishdīn ibn Kurayb. I asked: \"Is he stronger, or is Muḥammad ibn Kurayb stronger?\" He replied: \"There is not much difference between them, but Rishdīn ibn Kurayb is more preferable (*arjaḥ*) in my estimation.\"\n\nHe [al-Tirmidhī] said: And I asked Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl [al-Bukhārī] about this, and he said: \"Muḥammad ibn Kurayb is more preferable (*arjaḥ*) than Rishdīn ibn Kurayb.\"\n\nHe [al-Tirmidhī] said: **The position held by me is that of Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: Rishdīn ibn Kurayb is more preferable and more senior. He met Ibn ʿAbbās and saw him. The two of them are brothers, and both have narrations that are considered *munkar* (disliked or rejected).\"**\n\n---\n\n### Notes on the Hadith:\n\nThis narration describes the noble practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allāh be upon him) of pausing to breathe twice while drinking, which is a well-known etiquette (*adab*) of drinking in Islamic tradition. The chain of narration, however, is classified as *gharīb* by Imām al-Tirmidhī (may Allāh have mercy on him), as it is known only through Rishdīn ibn Kurayb. The concluding portion of the text records a scholarly discussion among the eminent hadith critics—al-Tirmidhī, al-Dārimī, and al-Bukhārī (may Allāh have mercy on them all)—regarding the relative reliability of the two brothers, Rishdīn and Muḥammad ibn Kurayb."
"1953","Aishah narrated:\"The Prophet would accept gifts and he would give something in return"
"1954","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"Whoever is not grateful to the people"
"1955","Abu Sa'eed narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"Whoever is not grateful to the people"
"1956","Abu Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"Your smiling in the face of your brother is charity"
"1957","Al-Bara bin Azib narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"Whoever gives someone some milk or silver"
"1958","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"When a man was walking on the road"
"1959","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said :\"When a man narrates a narration"
"1960","Asma bint Abi Bakr said:\" O the Messenger of Allah! I have nothing except what was given to me by (my husband) Az-Zubair"
"1961","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet said:\"Generosity is close to Allah"
"1962","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Two traits are not combined in a believer: Stinginess and bad manners"
"1963","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"The believer is naively noble and the stingy person is deceitfully treacherous"
"1964","Abu Mas'ud Al-Ansari narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"A man's spending on his family is charity"
"1965","Thawban narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"The most virtuous of the Dinar is the Dinar spent by a man on his dependants"
"1966","Abu Shuraih Al-'Adawf said:\"My eyes saw the Messenger of Allah"
"1967","Abu Shuraih Al-Kabi narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:: \"Hospitality is for three days"
"1968","Safwan bin Sulaim narrated that the Prophet said:\"The one who looks after a widow and a poor person is like the Mujahid in the cause of Allah"
"1969","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Every good is charity. Indeed among the good is to meet your brother with a smiling face"
"1970","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Abide by truthfulness. For indeed truthfulness leads to righteousness. And indeed righteousness leads to Paradise. A man continues telling the truth and trying hard to tell the truth until he is recorded with Allah as a truthful person. Refrain from falsehood. For indeed falsehood leads to wickedness"
"1971","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"When the slave (of Allah) lies"
"1972","Aishah narrated:\"There was no behavior more hated to the Messenger of Allah than lying. A man would lie in narrating something in the presence of the Prophet"
"1973","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Al-Fuhsh is not present in anything but it mars it"
"1974","Abdullah bin 'Amr said; \"The Messenger of Allah said:\"The best of you are those best in conduct.' And the Prophet was not one who was obscene"
"1975","Samurah bin Jundab narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Do not curse yourselves with Allah's curse"
"1976","Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"The believer does not insult the honor of others"
"1977","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that a man cursed the wind in the presence of the Prophet"
"1978","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Learn enough about your lineage to facilitate keeping your ties of kinship. For indeed keeping the ties of kinship encourages affection among the relatives"
"1979","Abudullah bin 'Amr narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"No supplication is more readily responded to"
"1980","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"(The burden of) what is said by the two who vilify each other is upon the one who initiated it"
"1981","Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Do not vilify the dead (and) by that harm the living"
"1982","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Verbally abusing the Muslim is disobedience and fighting him is disbelief.\" Zubaid said:\"I said to Abu Wa'il: 'Did you hear it from 'Abdullah?' He said: 'Yes"
"1983","Ali narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Indeed in Paradise there are chambers"
"1984","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"How wonderful it is for one of them that he obeys Allah and fulfills the rights of his master.\" Meaning the slave. And Ka'b said: \"Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth"
"1985","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"There shall be upon dunes of musk- I think he said: On the Day of Judgment- a slave who fulfills Allah's right and the right of his patron (master)"
"1986","Abu Dharr said:\"The Messenger of Allah said to me: 'Have Taqwa of Allah wherever you are"
"1987","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Beware of Zann (suspicion)"
"1988","Anas narrated:\" The Messenger of Allah used to mingle with us such that he said to my younger brother: 'O Abu 'Umair! What did the Nughair do?"
"1989","Abu Hurairah narrated:\"They said: 'O Messenger of Allah! You joke with us?' He said: 'Indeed I do not say except what is true.'\" (Hasan)"
"1990","Anas narrated:\"A man sought a mount from the Messenger of Allah who said: 'Indeed"
"1991","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"O possessor of two ears!\" Mahmud said: \"Abu Usamah said: 'He only meant it as a joke"
"1992","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever avoids lying while he is doing so falsely"
"1993","Ibn Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"It is enough sin for you that you never stop disputing"
"1994","Ibn Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Do not argue with your brother"
"1995","Aisha narrated:\"A man sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah while I was with him"
"1996","Muhammad bin Sirin narrated from Abu Hurairah - and I think he (narrated it from the Prophet) who said:\"Love your beloved moderately"
"1997","Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever has a mustard seed's weight of pride (arrogance) in his heart"
"1998","Abdullah narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever has a speck of pride (arrogance) in his heart"
"1999","Iylas bin Salamah bin Al-Akwa' narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah said:\"A man shall remain exalting himself until he is written among the tyrants"
"2000","Jubair bin Mut'im narrated from his father who said:\"They (meaning the people in general) told me that I was proud"
"2001","Abu Ad-Dardh narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Nothing is heavier on the believer's Scale on the Day of Judgment than good character. For indeed Allah"
"2002","Abu Ad-Dardh narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Nothing is placed on the Scale that is heavier than good character. Indeed the person with good character will have attained the rank of the person of fasting and prayer"
"2003","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah was asked about that for which people are admitted into Paradise the most"
"2004","Abu Wahb narrated that :'Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak explained good character"
"2005","Abu Al-Ahwas narrated from his father who said:\"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I stayed with a man who did not entertain me nor behave hospitably with me. Then he came to stay with me"
"2006","Hudhaifah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“Do not be a people without a will of your own"
"2007","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever visits the sick"
"2008","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Al-Haya is from faith"
"2009","Abdullah bin Sarjis Al-Muzam narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Taking the good route is a part of the twenty-four parts of Prophethood"
"2010","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah said to the Ashajj 'Abdul-Qais:\"Indeed there are two traits in you that Allah loves: Forbearance"
"2011","Abdullah-Muhaimin bin 'Abbas bin Sahl bin Sa'd As-Saidi narrated from his father"
"2012","Abu Ad-Darda narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever was given his share of gentleness"
"2013","Ibn 'Abbas narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah sent Mu'adh [bin Jabal] to Yemen"
"2014","Anas narrated:that \"I served the Prophet for ten years. He never said Uff and never blamed me by saying: 'Why did you do so' or why did you not do so?' And the Messenger Of Allah had the best character among all of the people. I never touched Khazz nor silk"
"2015","Abu Abdullah Al-Jadali narrated:\"I asked 'Aishah about the character of the Messenger of Allah. She said: 'He was not obscene"
"2016","Aishah narrated:\"I was not jealous of any wife of the Prophet as I was jealous of Khadijah"
"2017","Jabir narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Indeed the most beloved among you to me"
"2018","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"The believer is not one who curses others"
"2019","Abu Hurairah narrated that a man came to the Messenger of Allah and said:\"Teach me something that is not too much for me so that"
"2020","Sahl bim Mu'adh bin Anas Al-Juhani narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever suppresses his rage while he is able to unleash it"
"2021","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"No young person honors an elder due to his age"
"2022","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.A.W) said:\"The gates of Paradise are opened on Monday and Thursday. In them"
"2023","Abu Sa'eed narrated:\"Some persons from the Ansar asked for (something) from the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) and he gave them. They again asked him for (something)"
"2024","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\"Indeed among the worst of people to Allah"
"2025","Hammam bin Al-Harith said:\"Aman passed by Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman and it was said to him: \"This person conveys news about the people to the leaders.' So Hudaifah said: 'The Messenger of Allah said: 'The Qatat shall not enter paradise.'\" (Sahih)Sufyan said: \"The Qatat is the Nammam"
"2026","Abu Umamah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.A.W) said:\"Al-Haya' and Al-'Iy are two branches of faith"
"2027","Ibn 'Umar narrated that two men arrived during the time of the Messenger of Allah delivering an address. The people were amazed by their speech"
"2028","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Charity does not diminish wealth"
"2029","Ibn 'Umar narrated that Prophet said:\"Oppression shall be darkness on the Day of Judgment"
"2030","Abu Hurairah narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) never criticized any food. if he liked it"
"2031","Nafi' narrated that Ibn ‘Umar said:“The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) ascended the Minbar and called out with a raised voice: ’O you who accepted Islam with his tongue"
"2032","Abu Sa'eed narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\"There is no forbearance except for the one who stumbled"
"2033","Jabir narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\"Whoever is given a gift"
"2034","Usamah bin Zaid narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\"Whoever some good was done to him"
"2035","Qatadah bin An-Nu'man narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\"When Allah loves a slave"
